WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.217 --> 00:00:03.501
- Hey y'all, welcome to another
episode of Is This Okay?

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:06.060
Where we talk about things
and ask the question,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.316
is this okay?

00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:08.196
There we go.

00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:09.253
- I'm Jenny.

00:00:09.253 --> 00:00:10.470
- I'm Daysha.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.997
- I'm Nyla.

00:00:11.997 --> 00:00:12.830
- I'm Chris.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:13.663
- I'm Becky.

00:00:13.663 --> 00:00:15.757
- Today we're gonna talk
about a very scary topic,

00:00:15.757 --> 00:00:18.212
offensive Halloween costumes.

00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:19.315
This was good, that was great.

00:00:19.315 --> 00:00:20.632
(laughing)

00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:23.029
So this topic came about when I saw

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:25.405
a lot of articles being written about

00:00:25.405 --> 00:00:26.978
um, the Moana costume.

00:00:26.978 --> 00:00:28.258
It was like this costume,

00:00:28.258 --> 00:00:30.241
it was like you know full tats,

00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:31.737
and also you could see like the brown skin

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:32.801
underneath the tats,

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:33.634
so I would like to ask friends,

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:36.489
where do you draw the line
with offensive costumes?

00:00:36.489 --> 00:00:37.610
- Well for me personally,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.290
we see like sexy Indian

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.169
and then we also see the warrior.

00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:42.634
- When I see Asian costumes,

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.057
because a lot of it actually appeals

00:00:44.057 --> 00:00:45.353
to a very pan-Asian

00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:46.969
like oh Japanese and Chinese

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:48.689
they're like basically the same thing.

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:50.145
- For instance, like that MLK party,

00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:52.513
it was like come dressed as black people,

00:00:52.513 --> 00:00:54.186
and it's like, so then you have people

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:56.177
throwing up gang signs
and wearing baggy clothes

00:00:56.177 --> 00:00:57.010
and doing all this shit,

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.858
but when have you ever seen a party like,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.573
oh come dressed as white people.

00:01:00.573 --> 00:01:01.781
- If I were an offensive costume,

00:01:01.781 --> 00:01:03.061
that offended you or something,

00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:03.894
and I were to say to you,

00:01:03.894 --> 00:01:05.301
Chris it's just a costume,

00:01:05.301 --> 00:01:07.381
like get over it, it's just Halloween.

00:01:07.381 --> 00:01:09.709
Like, how would you react to that?

00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:10.941
- People are like it's just a costume,

00:01:10.941 --> 00:01:12.429
it's just a movie, it's just a game,

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:14.485
it's just a kids show,

00:01:14.485 --> 00:01:15.933
- It's just something.

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:19.797
- Because you, everyone thinks
it's just this one thing,

00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:24.717
it normalizes a lot of these
horrible like mindsets.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.205
Of like, oh I though black
people just look like this,

00:01:27.205 --> 00:01:28.325
I though Asian people just look like this,

00:01:28.325 --> 00:01:29.861
I thought Native people
just look like this

00:01:29.861 --> 00:01:30.725
- That's how Native Americans dress

00:01:30.725 --> 00:01:32.258
and you would not believe
the number of people

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.869
who actually, seriously,
in all seriousness

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:37.333
will ask me, but isn't that
the way Native Americans dress.

00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:39.733
- Is it just a matter
of doing your research?

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:41.237
- If someone came to me and said,

00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:42.933
you know, I want to dress
as Pocahontas for Halloween,

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:45.859
or I want to dress as
Crazy Horse for Halloween,

00:01:45.859 --> 00:01:46.692
I'd be like great.

00:01:46.692 --> 00:01:49.021
Learn about them, what
tribes they were from,

00:01:49.021 --> 00:01:50.061
what their traditions were,

00:01:50.061 --> 00:01:51.684
how they actually dressed,

00:01:51.684 --> 00:01:52.998
what their actual history was,

00:01:52.998 --> 00:01:55.109
not just I'm generically dressing in

00:01:55.109 --> 00:01:57.348
this weird little buckskin fringe

00:01:57.348 --> 00:01:59.781
and calling in Pocahontas.

00:01:59.781 --> 00:02:01.054
If you don't know anything

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.293
about the character you're dressing as,

00:02:03.293 --> 00:02:05.417
why do you want to you want
to dress as that character

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:06.358
in the first place.

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:07.877
Wouldn't you rather dress as something

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:09.109
that you are impressed by,

00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:11.741
that you do have some knowledge of.

00:02:11.741 --> 00:02:12.798
- Because then how can you say that you're

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:15.222
trying to honor those
people and that culture,

00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:17.478
if you didn't even take
two seconds to look it up.

00:02:17.478 --> 00:02:20.101
- This also like stems
from education though too,

00:02:20.101 --> 00:02:23.270
because I think like we
can all sit here and say

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.630
it takes two seconds to look it up

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.790
and it's easy peasy lemon squeezy for us,

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.030
because we're all culturally competent,

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.646
but I think think you
have these universities

00:02:32.646 --> 00:02:34.047
that have story after story after story

00:02:34.047 --> 00:02:36.430
of black face and cultural appropriation

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.439
and the deans excuse it,

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:38.598
so it's kind of like,

00:02:38.598 --> 00:02:39.941
well if the deans are excusing it,

00:02:39.941 --> 00:02:41.853
then its okay that we can do it.

00:02:41.853 --> 00:02:44.181
- Do you hold them accountable as much as

00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:45.910
you hold the school accountable

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.414
because they're not holding
the students accountable?

00:02:48.414 --> 00:02:51.014
- Yeah, I mean like, everyone
needs to be held accountable.

00:02:51.014 --> 00:02:53.158
Actually a lot of schools are telling kids

00:02:53.158 --> 00:02:55.926
to be cognizant of the fact
that they could be offensive

00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:58.526
and it's the kids that
are fighting against it.

00:02:58.526 --> 00:03:00.558
- It was a master actually,
it was a faculty member

00:03:00.558 --> 00:03:01.558
or a staff member.

00:03:01.558 --> 00:03:03.649
- Oh it was a staff member, well that's

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.207
even worse.

00:03:05.207 --> 00:03:07.599
- I think this just goes beyond,

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:10.478
like only white people doing it,

00:03:10.478 --> 00:03:13.366
I like that it is important,

00:03:13.366 --> 00:03:16.334
that we look deeper into this

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.710
and kind of dismantle systematic racism

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.894
and figure out ways, like

00:03:20.894 --> 00:03:23.558
Halloween itself, just
perpetuates all these stereotypes.

00:03:23.558 --> 00:03:26.415
It's not one specific group that does it.

00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:28.846
I think, you know, the holiday itself

00:03:28.846 --> 00:03:29.679
- It's not just race.

00:03:29.679 --> 00:03:31.022
- Yeah, it's not just race,

00:03:31.022 --> 00:03:32.662
it's misogyny, it's homophobia, it's all

00:03:32.662 --> 00:03:33.495
- Transphobia

00:03:33.495 --> 00:03:35.374
- Transphobia, you know, islamophobia,

00:03:35.374 --> 00:03:36.406
it all of these things.

00:03:36.406 --> 00:03:38.118
- So a while ago, I had a friend who

00:03:38.118 --> 00:03:40.654
dressed up as a black
celebrity that he really loved.

00:03:40.654 --> 00:03:41.662
He wore black face.

00:03:41.662 --> 00:03:43.438
And we were going to a party

00:03:43.438 --> 00:03:44.966
and we had a black friend of ours

00:03:44.966 --> 00:03:46.135
who thought it was really funny,

00:03:46.135 --> 00:03:48.854
was all about this idea,
thought the costume was great.

00:03:48.854 --> 00:03:51.734
And they talked about how,
just not upset anybody,

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.230
they would not put the photos on Facebook.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.894
Um, it still felt a little odd to me,

00:03:56.894 --> 00:03:59.350
but they were like if
no one else is seeing it

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.358
and everyone else here
knows that we are not racist

00:04:02.358 --> 00:04:04.534
and we all think the black face is funny

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:06.518
um then there's no harm, no foul.

00:04:06.518 --> 00:04:08.742
The black friend of mine essentially said

00:04:08.742 --> 00:04:11.582
don't be offended on
behalf of black people,

00:04:11.582 --> 00:04:13.294
like I'm saying, if I'm the only one here,

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:15.392
that sees this and I'm
comfortable with it,

00:04:15.392 --> 00:04:17.846
it should be, it should be okay.

00:04:17.846 --> 00:04:18.763
- Okay, so.

00:04:19.982 --> 00:04:21.814
(laughing)

00:04:21.814 --> 00:04:23.166
- Just because you

00:04:23.166 --> 00:04:25.127
and the fact that you are a black person

00:04:25.127 --> 00:04:26.558
thought that it was funny,

00:04:26.558 --> 00:04:30.623
like you have to understand
that as a whole community,

00:04:30.623 --> 00:04:31.878
that sets us back.

00:04:31.878 --> 00:04:32.967
- I feel very mixed about this,

00:04:32.967 --> 00:04:35.246
because like you're allowed
to have your opinion,

00:04:35.246 --> 00:04:36.550
like we're all individuals and like

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.174
Asian people, black people, like we all

00:04:39.174 --> 00:04:40.817
don't have don't have a hive mind,

00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:43.999
so we all don't have to think
the same way about things.

00:04:43.999 --> 00:04:45.414
- Again, both people are fine,

00:04:45.414 --> 00:04:46.782
you can live in the same world,

00:04:46.782 --> 00:04:48.070
but the person that's not offended

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.646
has no right to tell the other person

00:04:49.646 --> 00:04:50.910
that they shouldn't be offended.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.198
- Okay, even if he's the only
black person at that party,

00:04:53.198 --> 00:04:55.015
you all live in the world

00:04:55.015 --> 00:04:58.215
and everybody else is
taking that experience

00:04:58.215 --> 00:05:00.406
and this sort of assumption
that this is okay

00:05:00.406 --> 00:05:02.382
back into the real world

00:05:02.382 --> 00:05:04.854
and that feeds into a continuing problem.

00:05:04.854 --> 00:05:07.335
- It seems like the next question is

00:05:07.335 --> 00:05:09.382
then what do we do about

00:05:09.382 --> 00:05:10.462
how they keep happening

00:05:10.462 --> 00:05:11.527
and it seemed like you guys

00:05:11.527 --> 00:05:13.926
were saying that you want the schools

00:05:13.926 --> 00:05:15.359
to take more responsibility,

00:05:15.359 --> 00:05:17.662
but at what point can the school then,

00:05:17.662 --> 00:05:20.023
after you educate what
are you going to say,

00:05:20.023 --> 00:05:22.583
I mean that you have to
approve your costume with us.

00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:24.518
- For instance, I went to a school

00:05:24.518 --> 00:05:27.086
and somebody had wrote the
word nigger on the wall.

00:05:27.086 --> 00:05:29.078
I think they said I wish
all niggers would die

00:05:29.078 --> 00:05:29.911
or something like that

00:05:29.911 --> 00:05:32.711
and so instead of like specifically going

00:05:32.711 --> 00:05:34.057
after the individual,

00:05:34.057 --> 00:05:35.567
the school then said okay

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.446
somebody clearly thought
that this was a space

00:05:38.446 --> 00:05:40.175
in which they could say
something like that,

00:05:40.175 --> 00:05:42.596
so we're going to reevaluate the space

00:05:42.596 --> 00:05:44.142
and we're going to create programming

00:05:44.142 --> 00:05:45.665
to talk about these things

00:05:45.665 --> 00:05:48.039
and to create a different
kind of environment,

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:49.486
that we actually want to foster

00:05:49.486 --> 00:05:50.830
so that no one ever thinks

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.369
that this is a space that they
can write that kind of stuff.

00:05:53.369 --> 00:05:55.718
- It's a tough issue that
I hope we all think about.

00:05:55.718 --> 00:05:56.551
- Yeah.

00:05:56.551 --> 00:05:58.790
- So you all already know what to do.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.702
Leave your comments in the
comments section below.

00:06:01.702 --> 00:06:02.871
- Be nice to each other.

00:06:02.871 --> 00:06:04.302
- Yeah, be nice to each other.

00:06:04.302 --> 00:06:06.110
It's the internet you guys.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.502
Love one another, gees.

00:06:08.502 --> 00:06:10.726
And we will see you next week.

00:06:10.726 --> 00:06:12.976
(laughing)

